# Repository-wide build excludes, for any image built with this repository as its context.
#
# This file used to be `*` plus re-includes for `symbolu/` and one requirements path: rules
# written for deploy/gke/Dockerfile and for nothing else. Docker reads the .dockerignore at
# the CONTEXT ROOT, so those rules applied to every root-context build and put every other
# build's sources outside its own context — the Symbol-U API service failed with
# `"/pyproject.toml": not found`, and neither deployment image could be built at all
# (docs/audits/ugence_governance_studio_p3e/BUILD_CONTEXT_EXCLUSION_DEFECT.json).
#
# Those rules now live in deploy/gke/Dockerfile.dockerignore, which BuildKit reads in
# preference to this file, so that image's context is unchanged. What follows excludes
# only what no image wants. A build needing more than this carries its own
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`; deployment/governance-studio and
# deployment/governed-runtime-worker already do.
#
# deployment/governance-studio/ci/verify_build_context.py checks, offline and on every CI
# run, that each Dockerfile's COPY sources and the root build's declared inputs survive
# whichever of these files its build actually reads.

# Version control and CI metadata
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Dependencies and virtual environments
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
**/.venv/

# Build output and caches
dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.vite/
coverage/
**/coverage/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# Secrets and credentials: never in a build context, never in a layer
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
**/secrets/
